.TH DECODEIMAGE 1 2026-10月 "" "Decode a grayscale image on the disk"
.SH NAME
decodeImage \- decodeImage(start, wavFile,
    <i>size</i> = <span style='color: green;'>364</span>,
    <i>lines</i> = <span style='color: green;'>512</span>,
    <i>white</i> = <span style='color: green;'>1</span>,
    <i>gamma</i> = <span style='color: green;'>1</span>,
    <i>percentile</i> = <span style='color: blue !important;'>NULL</span>,
    <i>palette</i> = <span style='color: #808080;'><strong>'gray'</strong></span>,
    <i>smooth</i> = <span style='color: green;'>0</span>,
    <i>luminous</i> = <span style='color: blue !important;'>FALSE</span>,
    <i>report</i> = <span style='color: blue !important;'>FALSE</span>)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIdecodeImage(start, wavFile,
    <i>size</i> = <span style='color: green;'>364</span>,
    <i>lines</i> = <span style='color: green;'>512</span>,
    <i>white</i> = <span style='color: green;'>1</span>,
    <i>gamma</i> = <span style='color: green;'>1</span>,
    <i>percentile</i> = <span style='color: blue !important;'>NULL</span>,
    <i>palette</i> = <span style='color: #808080;'><strong>'gray'</strong></span>,
    <i>smooth</i> = <span style='color: green;'>0</span>,
    <i>luminous</i> = <span style='color: blue !important;'>FALSE</span>,
    <i>report</i> = <span style='color: blue !important;'>FALSE</span>)\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
the scan line period and the pixel clock are measured from the waveform data
itself (see the ``decode.report`` function), the legacy ``windowSize`` and
``offset`` parameters of the decoder are not used any more.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBstart\fB \fR\- . the data start position on the raw wav file
.PP
.PP
\fBwavFile\fB \fR\- . the file path of the wav file
.PP
.PP
\fBsize\fB \fR\- 364. the pixel cells (the image rows) inside a single scan line, default 364
.PP
.PP
\fBlines\fB \fR\- 512. the number of the scan lines (the image columns), default 512
.PP
.PP
\fBwhite\fB \fR\- 1. the white point gain of the rendering, 1 means no adjustment
.PP
.PP
\fBgamma\fB \fR\- 1. the gamma correction of the rendering, 1 means no correction
.PP
.PP
\fBpercentile\fB \fR\- NULL. the black point and the white point percentiles of the auto levels
.PP
.PP
\fBpalette\fB \fR\- 'gray'. the palette name of the pseudo color rendering
.PP
.PP
\fBsmooth\fB \fR\- 0. the radius of the across scan line smoothing, 0 for disable.
the smoothing is disabled by default because it reduces the edge
contrast of the decoded image and makes it look blurred
.PP
.PP
\fBluminous\fB \fR\- FALSE. render the image as the pseudo color image
.PP
.PP
\fBreport\fB \fR\- FALSE. print the empirical analysis report of the data section
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a bitmap image object
.PP
.SH FILES
.PP
SMRUCC/R#.declare_function.decodeImage at decoder.R:line 26
.PP
